    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d526-a2">

                <pb facs="0608" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg520"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron de Lynden to Mr. Garrett.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs,<lb/>Consular and Commercial
                                Bureau</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Hague</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-01-27"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January 27, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Chargé d’affaires</hi>: Referring to the letter
                    from his excellency Mr. Stanford Newel, dated September 5 last, I have the honor
                    to send you herewith a note from the minister of waterstaat, commerce, and
                    industry, from whence you will observe that Her Majesty’s Government, to its
                    regret, can not consent to the request of the United States Government conveyed
                    in the above-mentioned note.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bn. Melvil de
                    Lynden.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
